  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 116 of the laws of 2016 authorizing Richard Insogna, Jr. to take the competitive civil service examination and be placed on the eligible list for appointment as a full-time police officer for the village of Fort Plain, county of Montgomery, in relation to technical corrections thereto",
    "basePrintNo": "S973",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S973-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §§1 & 2, Chap 116 of 2016",
    "lawSection": "Civil Service",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S973\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\n\nAn act to amend chapter 116 of the laws of 2016 authorizing Richard\nInsogna, Jr. to take the competitive civil service examination and be\nplaced on the eligible list for appointment as a full-time police\nofficer for the village of Fort Plain, county of Montgomery, in\nrelation to technical corrections thereto\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL :\n\nThe purpose of the bill is make technical amendments to chapter 116 of\nthe laws of 2016 to authorize Richard Insogna Sr. to take the\ncompetitive civil service examination and be placed on the eligible\nlist for appointment as a full-time police officer for the village for\nFort Plain in the County of Montgomery.\n\n SUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS :\n\nSection one and two make technical amendments to chapter 116 of the\nlaws of 2016 to authorize Richard lnsogna Sr. to sit for the civil\nservice exam and be placed on a eligibility list for a full time\npolice officer position in the village of Fort Plain subject to merit\nand fitness requirements.\n\nSection three establishes the effective date.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nUnder the Civil Service Law, as proscribed under Section 58, no\nindividual may take the civil service examination, nor be eligible for\na civil service appointment as a police officer, at the age of 35 or\nolder. Due to this limitation, the village of Fort Plain Police\nDepartment has requested legislation to permit one of their part-time\nofficers, Richard Insogna, Sr., to be eligible to take the civil\nservice examination since he is currently older than 35 years old.\n\nIn small rural areas, it is difficult to attract or maintain qualified\napplicants to fill such positions. Upon Richard Insogna, Sr. passing\nthe examination, this would qualify him to fill the vacant full-time\nposition within the village of Fort Plain Police Department.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nNew bill: chapter amendment for chapter 116 of the laws of 2016.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS :\n\nTo be determined.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nTakes effect on the same date and in the same manner as Chapter 116 of\nthe laws of 2016 takes effect.\n",
